# Raw per-run output: test logs, Playwright traces and videos, scratch files.
# Large, machine-specific, and reproducible — nothing here is worth a diff.
runs/

*.tmp

# Generated by qa-map.mjs from the repo itself. Rebuilt in under a second,
# and stale the moment anyone commits — regenerate rather than diff it.
map.txt
map.json

# Per-agent scenario briefs, written by qa-partition.mjs from the plan at the
# start of every implement stage. Regenerated, never read twice, and committing
# them puts a diff of throwaway files in every pull request.
briefs/
*.trace.zip

# Deliberately NOT ignored, and worth committing:
#   sessions/   the run ledger — stages, timings, and every decision a human
#               made. "row lock, not optimistic version" is a record you want
#               six months from now.
#   traces/     what each agent concluded, rejected and wanted. This is how you
#               write eval cases from real runs instead of from imagination.
#
# At trace.level: full these can grow. If that becomes a problem, prune old
# traces rather than ignoring the directory — losing them costs you the only
# evidence of how the agents actually behaved.
